Correctness defect at input.rs:2: dereferencing bytes.as_ptr() is undefined behavior for an empty slice, which is a valid input under the requested contract. A SAFETY comment cannot establish a missing dereference precondition. SAFE-01 calls for the equivalent safe implementation; ERR-01 supports Option because absence has an obvious cause:

/// Returns the first byte, or None if the slice is empty.
pub fn first(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<u8> {
    bytes.first().copied()
}

Callers must handle None. This removes the unsafe block and represents the empty case without a panic or fabricated byte. Relevant checks would cover empty and nonempty slices; none were executed in this read-only review.

